From 629ce06a3cd61d1f5d6ed50008b30ad7ec33026b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 06:49:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0198 -- an IRQ-safe uclock(): each PIT read after
 the first runs with interrupts off

Why: DJGPP's uclock() latches PIT channel 0 and reads its two count bytes with
interrupts on, and the SB ISR times itself on the same counter. An SB IRQ
between the main thread's latch and its byte reads finds the 8254
mid-sequence: the ISR's own latch is ignored and its two reads return the
main thread's leftover byte plus a live one. The ISR's delta is then garbage
-- the 22-54 ms isr_max outliers (hub docs/timing.md) -- and it biases
isr_ns_per_write, a judged figure since CAP3c.

What: __wrap_uclock(), for a program linked with -Wl,--wrap=uclock, so
every uclock() call in it (the application, this library, libc) comes here.
Calls after the first run __real_uclock() with interrupts off and EFLAGS
restored after, so the latch and both byte reads cannot be split by an IRQ.
The FIRST call runs with the caller's interrupt flag untouched: it
reprograms channel 0 and then waits for the BIOS tick to change, which
never happens at IF=0. SDL_DOSUclockWrapStats() reports how many calls took
each path.

The wrapper is its own object: __real_uclock must be a strong reference (a
weak one does not pull libc's uclock.o out of the archive and resolves to
0; checked with the DJGPP toolchain), and a program linked without the flag
never pulls this object in. Reporting-side change only: no behaviour change
beyond the few microseconds each read holds interrupts off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h       | 10 ++++
 src/timer/dos/SDL_dosuclockwrap.c | 83 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 93 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/timer/dos/SDL_dosuclockwrap.c

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h
index 1729dfc7f..ef666915f 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosident.h
@@ -154,6 +154,16 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL_DOSAudioGetDSPVersionMinor(void);
  */
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL_DOSAudioGetResolvedDMAChannel(void);
 
+/**
+ * dosags patch 0198: the IRQ-safe uclock() wrapper's counts. first = calls that ran DJGPP's uclock()
+ * with the interrupt flag as the caller left it (the first call, which reprograms PIT channel 0 and
+ * waits on the BIOS tick); wrapped = later calls, each made with interrupts off. Both 0 when the program
+ * was linked without -Wl,--wrap=uclock (the wrapper is then never called). Any pointer may be NULL.
+ *
+ * \since SDL 3 -- dosags workspace-local patch 0198, 2026-09-25.
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSUclockWrapStats(Uint32 *first, Uint32 *wrapped);
+
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
 #endif
diff --git a/src/timer/dos/SDL_dosuclockwrap.c b/src/timer/dos/SDL_dosuclockwrap.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ce4a5d7b3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/timer/dos/SDL_dosuclockwrap.c
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
